ps://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2022-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... We also find\\n\\nthis claim in Rebecca Walkowitz's seminal study of the born-translated novel, which maps\\n\\npatterns of global circulation across multiple languages and with a specific attention to the\\n\\ncreative shifts within and between popular genres. Not coincidentally, this recuperation and\\n\\nrevival of genre as ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327409406_Planetary_Figurations_Intensive_Genre_in_World_Literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... Austin, Mario Ortiz Robles argues that the language of the novel is paramount and that the current emphasis on the representational and physical aspects of the novel tends to obscure this fact. He provides brilliant original readings of five major Victorian novels: Dickens's Our Mutual Friend, Brontë ... \",\"title\":\"https://english.wisc.edu/department-life/faculty-bookshelf/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Smith/Books in Canada First Novel Award, the U.S. The Lambda Literary Award, and was named a Notable Book by the American Library Association. Selvadurai's second novel Cinnamon Gardens was published in Canada, the U.K, the USA and was translated into 6 languages: Italian, French ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d2\"},\"ref\":\"d2\",\"snippet\":\" ... She has translated three novels by the Italian writer Domenico Starnone, and is the editor of The Penguin Book of Italian Short Stories. A contributor for over twenty-five years toThe New Yorker magazine, she has published critical essays on authors including Ovid, Dante, Primo Levi, Alessandro Manzoni ... \",\"title\":\"https://barnard.edu/profiles/jhumpa-lahiri\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b0f632b0ffd3578fb385caf6aabf4cc4cc7565b40a0d6546247745ac591e8342\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"08aabfa3df178e09fdf9782e7681f06f92d5dbfde43b6cf40c3448440f3836aa\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"award founded 2000s novel translated over twenty five languages contender\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_aede7cd618504a4095226bf5"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize was created in 1969, so that doesn't fit. But the Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (2000s). However, Obioma's novels were shortlisted for the regular Booker Prize, not the International one.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the award is the Man Asian Literary Prize (created 2007). Let me check the Man Asian Literary Prize winners and shortlist in the 2010s, and whether any shortlisted book was translated into 25+ languages.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize winners list 2010 2011 2012 2013\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize shortlist translated 25 languages\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize Wikipedia history\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_8f67cc30c96045bbae1203db","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"